            {
                "entry_id": "3e517f15-2ca2-37a8-b3bd-5d610a783ffd",
                "word": "nativiste",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "8e436c3c-54c3-4cb4-8a6d-0f81377a4ba2",
                        "entry_id": "3e517f15-2ca2-37a8-b3bd-5d610a783ffd",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "masculine",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "nativistes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3a9336eb-4108-33f6-b9c8-38d6c48bd4c7",
                        "entry_id": "3e517f15-2ca2-37a8-b3bd-5d610a783ffd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Relatif au nativisme psychologique."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "79f4818f-39e3-438e-a4bc-31bb3ef65b12",
                                "sense_id": "3a9336eb-4108-33f6-b9c8-38d6c48bd4c7",
                                "text": "À cette conception empiriste, s’oppose la doctrine nativiste de J. Müller qui pense que la représentation de l’espace est une idée innée et non une perception."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e9356439-d5af-4ee3-bd74-4ffe806585c8",
                                "sense_id": "3a9336eb-4108-33f6-b9c8-38d6c48bd4c7",
                                "text": "Le succès de cette hypothèse n’est pas sans lien avec les conceptions nativistes du langage et de son acquisition et la vision des relations entre l’inné et l’acquis développées dans le courant de la linguistique formelle et par ailleurs largement médiatisées."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3847f17c-9c11-4ea5-885a-f0b7cc696e3d",
                                "sense_id": "3a9336eb-4108-33f6-b9c8-38d6c48bd4c7",
                                "text": "Le linguiste Noam Chomsky [1965] propose alors la théorie de la grammaire universelle selon laquelle l’esprit, dès la naissance, est doté de structures permettant de saisir les principes de toute grammaire humaine. Sa perspective nativiste est contestée par le courant constructiviste, notamment incarné par le psychologue Jean Piaget."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "75c25a63-5038-34b3-96ce-c9a246940652",
                        "entry_id": "3e517f15-2ca2-37a8-b3bd-5d610a783ffd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Relatif au nativisme politique."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6460cd5d-b89e-4c3d-bb0b-aeacf27796e2",
                                "sense_id": "75c25a63-5038-34b3-96ce-c9a246940652",
                                "text": "C’est cette Église irlandaise qui doit faire face aux premières attaques du mouvement nativiste protestant qui voit en elle une cinquième colonne vaticane."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b9163935-6345-4e62-89f2-996c60e18544",
                                "sense_id": "75c25a63-5038-34b3-96ce-c9a246940652",
                                "text": "Dans la première moitié du XIXe siècle, l’arrivée massive de catholiques européens et le développement d'un fort sentiment « nativiste » anticatholique conduisent la hiérarchie à prendre clairement position."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "52fea607-cc80-4c0e-bfce-8ff8eeeb0976",
                                "sense_id": "75c25a63-5038-34b3-96ce-c9a246940652",
                                "text": "Au-delà de cette critique, il n'en reste pas moins que Machete entache l’image du mouvement nativiste grâce à la moquerie."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3b047f7f-323b-4f42-9560-d26d3cfaf4ef",
                                "sense_id": "75c25a63-5038-34b3-96ce-c9a246940652",
                                "text": "L’agenda du gouvernement Meloni est ainsi sans doute moins nataliste que nativiste. Le ministre de l’agriculture, Francesco Lollobrigida, également beau-frère de Giorgia Meloni, a ainsi déclaré récemment : « Nous ne pouvons pas nous résigner à l’idée d’un remplacement ethnique : les Italiens ont moins d’enfants alors remplaçons-les par d’autres. Ce n’est pas la voie à suivre. »"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "65c68a9e-8bf7-3586-a213-dbc16e8555e5",
                        "entry_id": "3e517f15-2ca2-37a8-b3bd-5d610a783ffd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Relatif au fait que le président Barack Obama est, ou non, un natif des États-Unis."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "05250b99-7016-4d52-b35a-997d4e05f1d4",
                                "sense_id": "65c68a9e-8bf7-3586-a213-dbc16e8555e5",
                                "text": "Le magnat de l'immobilier, qui grimpe dans les sondages après avoir repris à son compte la théorie du « complot nativiste » (birther), était intervenu quelques minutes avant le président à la télévision pour aborder la question."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "df0da430-cf74-420d-a9b6-218f07c14f63",
                        "source_entry_id": "3e517f15-2ca2-37a8-b3bd-5d610a783ffd",
                        "target_lang_word": "nativistic",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "nativistic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a109122c-978b-3ed6-b525-22b37548d896",
                                        "entry_id": "98a4018e-03a7-31f7-9d6e-bf45729a42f6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In agreement with the philosophy of nativism."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "20c5ba0d-50b5-41c7-8012-1e3d1cc77848",
                                                "sense_id": "a109122c-978b-3ed6-b525-22b37548d896",
                                                "text": "He wrote that the “nativistic American mentality, born of ignorance and nurtured by malice,” insisted on stereotypes of Italian Americans as either “spaghetti-twirling, opera-bellowing buffoons in undershirts (as in the TV commercial with its famous line, ‘That’sa spicy meatball’), or swarthy, sinister hoods in garish suits, shirts and ties.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c5e8b411-724d-4e8b-83e1-d92b6a4e95a6",
                        "source_entry_id": "3e517f15-2ca2-37a8-b3bd-5d610a783ffd",
                        "target_lang_word": "birther",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "birther",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "51ada0ce-aece-398b-9742-04239c4dc43b",
                                        "entry_id": "aca604b4-089d-3b57-8369-75339f634853",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who gives birth."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b4d864b-34b3-4b40-94df-f0ec3b6f6d01",
                                                "sense_id": "51ada0ce-aece-398b-9742-04239c4dc43b",
                                                "text": "[…] she couldn't be an \"easy birther.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e7d62904-f8eb-4a95-be76-06ef5408180f",
                                                "sense_id": "51ada0ce-aece-398b-9742-04239c4dc43b",
                                                "text": "Liz Buttle, Britain's oldest birther, lied about not taking fertility drugs and didn't conceive her 2-month-old boy in the usual way as she insisted."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d2fd903b-6fee-327f-a139-2433808d8166",
                                        "entry_id": "aca604b4-089d-3b57-8369-75339f634853",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A believer in the conspiracy theory that Barack Obama, 44th president of the United States (2009–2017), is not a natural-born US citizen, and was therefore ineligible for the presidency under the United States Constitution (Article II, Section 1)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US",
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ced69899-b858-48fa-9929-2214990f4b22",
                                                "sense_id": "d2fd903b-6fee-327f-a139-2433808d8166",
                                                "text": "I confess I do have some sympathy for the \"birthers,\" though. As an outsider, it's hard to distinguish between the zany arguments that get official approval by the conservative establishment --- things like Bill Ayers, Michelle Obama's infamous \"whitey\" tape, the claim that Obama is a closet Marxist --- and those arguments that are considered beyond the pale."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b2cdb844-cb9d-48c5-b7e4-59f68a894720",
                                                "sense_id": "d2fd903b-6fee-327f-a139-2433808d8166",
                                                "text": "Senator Dick Durbin has suggested that the birthers and the health care protesters are one and the same; we don’t know how many of the protesters are birthers, but it wouldn’t be surprising if it’s a substantial fraction."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd4be50c-c825-4346-a4f0-74a26e20e95f",
                                                "sense_id": "d2fd903b-6fee-327f-a139-2433808d8166",
                                                "text": "Earlier this month, columnist and birther Frank Gaffney, Rep. Pete Hoekstra, R-Mich., the ranking Republican on the Intelligence Committee, and others held a news conference on Capitol Hill to release a report on Muslim religious law entitled \"Shariah: The Threat to America.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c135066e-537b-3782-be03-076372b48c1a",
                                        "entry_id": "aca604b4-089d-3b57-8369-75339f634853",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "More generally, anyone who questions the eligibility of a candidate for office based on their citizenship status."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US",
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e199c29-23ad-4420-b9df-1885f436eb84",
                                                "sense_id": "c135066e-537b-3782-be03-076372b48c1a",
                                                "text": "[see title]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1dedc106-e29a-4e4b-aea0-f76b0f3f8b5a",
                                                "sense_id": "c135066e-537b-3782-be03-076372b48c1a",
                                                "text": "On Thursday, he started floating a new birther lie about Sen. Kamala Harris, who, if elected, would be the first Black and Asian American vice president."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "birther",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "88986567-4579-3b75-8f22-e561d0bb0783",
                                        "entry_id": "9c7b9e82-923b-3745-b16b-d27b03d57556",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To question the eligibility of a candidate for office or the location of one's birth."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US",
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
